<h2><a name="5"></a><div class="storyTitle">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;NoV scores a serverwide first- Emperor Ssraeshza ninja looted and rifts stolen.  <!-- <a href="?cat=1" title="category: General"><span class="storyCategory">[General]</span></a>-->

<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;
<span class="storyAuthor">rejekted 

<!-- &#99;on&#110;e&#99;&#116;bri&#97;&#110;&#64;&#121;&#97;&#104;&#111;o.&#99;&#111;&#109;</span>
 @ <a href="index.php?m=200209#5">11:25:58</a>
-->
 - Tuesday, September 24, 2002 
</div>
</h2>
<div class="storyContent">
Before I get into the issue at hand, let me introduce myself to some of you who might not know me too well. I go by the name Injekted in Everquest. I've been playing a rogue on fennin ro for quite a few years- since Kunark was released, I believe. During my time in everquest, I've been a part of a fair amount of server firsts, including the avatar of war, tunare, blood of ssra, etc. I've seen some good kills in my time, where a guild prepares for weeks, even months to finally "get it right" and down the beast. I've seen some messy kills, where if the fight had lasted even an instant longer, all would have been lost. There have also been the rare occasions when a level 20 ogre hovers over your monster's corpse, praying that his /loot hotkey wins it for him. In every instance I've seen, that loot has been transferred to the rightful owner by GMs- to the person awarded the item from said mob. <br />
<br />
Something big happened tonight- something I've never seen before.<br />
<br />
I generally make it a rule to never post an update that flames another guild. Hell, it states in our guild policy that our members are forbidden to flame any individual, regardless of tag. However, this goes beyond standard policy. This evening, The Mystical Order broke more rules of Verant policy than I've ever seen. Fuck common courtesy or "playing nice", the phrases don't even register in their 3 year old childish minds. <br />
<br />
This evening, we started prepping for Emperor Ssraeshza. It was going to be our second kill, a notable feat for us, so we wanted to be ready. We had been the only ones in force in the zone since early morning. Quickly our forces grew, and by 5 pm EST, we had 60+ guilded in the zone. At the time, TMO had 20-something guilded and 1 cleric online, obviously not enough to even hurt the Blood. We then killed a few rares for some Insignias, and clicked up to the blood room. TMO still had less than 30 in the zone. As time went by, we discussed our strategy for killing emp, and started setting up groups. By the time we were ready to engage blood, TMO starts SWARMING in behind us en masse, mass clicking the portal up to blood. At that point, we engaged. Somehow, we were able to fend off the mass-inspecting, chain-horrifying-clerics, mez-breaking fiends, and defeat the emperor. To the clerics, I salute you. Damn fine job even with that mess. Enchanters, nice work, even with the broken mezzes.<br />
<br />
To the 40 TMO who took part in this tragedy, plooted and destroyed approx 25 rifts (sinadel, riverstorm, others), plooted an acrylia handled broadswoard (sinadel), plooted a gebron's demented cloak (edited: Maestrolo, confirmed) mez-breakers, chain-inspecters, cleric-horrifyers, and those who planned this, supported this, and ABUSED your rights to EXIST in the everquest world, fuck you.<br />
<br />
We're IN vex thal, we're gonna eventually kill aten ha ra, we're gonna kill emp, seru, vulak, whatever. we're gonna get 60 people online at 5 est on a weekday, and all those things you try to keep us from doing, we're gonna do it. Keep trying to cockblock, get your kicks while you can, keep wasting your time. We don't do it to compete with you. That's not our style. We do it for us.<br />
<br />
To the TMO members that guildremoved themselves in shame of their guild, congratulations, it must feel like being set free, eh? To the rest of TMO- once you get back from your suspensions, get cozy on your knees, because it's gonna take a lot of sucking up to win back the respect of ANYONE on this, and any server that holds people who have at least half a brain.<br />
<br />
Good luck, TMO, in your quest for trust and mercy from the rest of us. <br />
Here's to hoping the GMs come to the understanding that TMO is a guild full of those level 20 ogres hovering over that uber mob's corpse, and do something about it. <br />
<br />
<br />
-rejekted the rogue

</div>

